    "summary": "Model completed and passed all L1/L2/L3 checks.\n\nBridge: single simply-supported span, 30 m centre-to-centre of bearings, deck width 10 m. Three precast prestressed small-box girders (C40), midspan section h=1.6 m, b_top=2.40 m, single-girder A=1.13893 m², I=0.35492 m⁴; three-girder A=3.41679 m², I=1.06475 m⁴. Girder self-weight only: w=88.836 kN/m (γ=26 kN/m³), m=9.056 t/m; Ec=32500 MPa.\n\nSupports: abutments 0 and 1, each with 6 plain laminated elastomeric bearings (2 per girder end × 3 girders), 300×400 mm plan, 5 internal layers × 8 mm. Modeled as zero-length springs: S=10.714, Kv=8.518×10⁶ kN/m, Kh=18 000 kN/m per line, vertical/longitudinal spring, rotation free.\n\nLoading: Highway Class II (JTG D60-2015), two-way, carriageway 9 m, 2 design lanes; qk=7.875 kN/m, Pk=240 kN per span, xi=1.00, μ=0.2006 (f1=3.4017 Hz).\n\nResults: first vertical bending frequency 3.402 Hz; self-weight support reactions 1332.5 + 1332.5 = 2665 kN (balances total self-weight); self-weight midspan moment 9994 kN·m; lane live-load max positive moment 6450 kN·m.\n\nRoot cause of the initial failure: the transverse lane-loading factor lane.xi had been accepted as 0.78 (the JTG D60-2015 Table 4.3.1-5 value for 3 lanes), but this bridge has only 2 design lanes, for which xi=1.00. Check L2-1 (recomputation of each parameter from the rule/code formulas) therefore failed without pinning a single decision. Setting lane.xi=1.00 and re-confirming lane.mu against the unchanged f1 fixed the model."
